{{!
    @template auth_emailasusername/signup_form

    Signup form presenting the email address as the username.

    The form class renders itself and hands the resulting markup over, so this
    template only places it. It exists because core derives the template name
    from the class name: auth_emailasusername\form\signup_form resolves to
    auth_emailasusername/signup_form when login/signup.php renders the form.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * formhtml - the rendered moodleform

    Example context (json):
    {
        "formhtml": "<form action=\"signup.php\" method=\"post\"></form>"
    }
}}
{{{ formhtml }}}
